# Circuitry environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/circuitry/.env (or wherever `cof setup`
# created one) and fill in the keys for the adapters and tool plugins you
# actually use. Every line below is optional: leave a line out (or unset)
# and `cof doctor` names exactly what is still missing the moment you try
# to use it. API keys never belong in config.json or in an orchestration
# document — see docs/guidebook/04-configuration.md.
#
# This file (once at ~/.config/circuitry/.env, mode 0600) is loaded
# automatically by every host entry point: the `cof` CLI, the TUI, the MCP
# server (`circuitry-mcp`), and the REST trigger service. A variable
# already set in the real environment always wins. The SDK
# (circuitry.api) does not load it automatically — an embedding program
# owns its own environment.
#
# Every placeholder line below is uncommented, so delete the ones you don't
# use before copying this to ~/.config/circuitry/.env — once there, every
# line present is loaded, and `cof doctor` / the setup wizard will treat
# each placeholder as a real, configured credential.
#
# Self-hosted adapters (ollama, vllm, llama.cpp, LM Studio, TGI without a
# reverse-proxy token) need no credentials and are not listed here.

# --- OpenAI ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# --- Anthropic ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here

# --- Google Gemini ---
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-api-key-here

# --- Groq ---
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your-key-here

# --- Mistral ---
MISTRAL_API_KEY=your-mistral-key-here

# --- Cohere ---
COHERE_API_KEY=your-cohere-key-here

# --- AI21 ---
AI21_API_KEY=your-ai21-key-here

# --- Together AI ---
TOGETHER_API_KEY=your-together-key-here

# --- Fireworks AI ---
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=your-fireworks-key-here

# --- DeepSeek ---
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your-deepseek-key-here

# --- xAI (Grok) ---
XAI_API_KEY=your-xai-key-here

# --- OpenRouter ---
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-key-here

# --- Perplexity ---
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=your-perplexity-key-here

# --- Hugging Face Inference ---
HF_TOKEN=hf_your-token-here

# --- Alibaba Qwen (DashScope) ---
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=your-dashscope-key-here

# --- NVIDIA NIM (build.nvidia.com) ---
NIM_API_KEY=nvapi-your-key-here

# --- Replicate ---
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=r8_your-token-here

# --- Databricks Model Serving ---
DATABRICKS_TOKEN=your-databricks-token-here
DATABRICKS_HOST=https://your-workspace.cloud.databricks.com

# --- Cloudflare Workers AI ---
CF_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token-here
CF_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id-here

# --- Azure OpenAI ---
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your-azure-openai-key-here
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.openai.azure.com

# --- IBM watsonx.ai ---
WATSONX_API_KEY=your-watsonx-api-key-here
WATSONX_PROJECT_ID=your-watsonx-project-id-here
# WATSONX_REGION=us-south          # optional, this is the built-in default
# WATSONX_API_VERSION=2024-03-14   # optional, this is the built-in default

# --- Tool plugins (credentials a `tool` effect reads at call time, not at
#     startup — only needed for the orchestrations that actually use them) ---
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-your-slack-bot-token-here
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your-github-token-here
NOTION_TOKEN=secret_your-notion-token-here
LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_your-linear-key-here
JIRA_URL=https://your-site.atlassian.net
JIRA_USER=your-email@example.com
JIRA_TOKEN=your-jira-api-token-here
# Shared by the gdrive and gcalendar plugins (a service-account JSON file path):
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/your-service-account.json
# Shared by the surrealdb tool plugin and the surrealdb persistence backend —
# SURREAL_TOKEN alone is enough; otherwise set both SURREAL_USER and SURREAL_PASS:
SURREAL_TOKEN=your-surrealdb-jwt-here
SURREAL_USER=your-surrealdb-user-here
SURREAL_PASS=your-surrealdb-password-here

# --- Circuitry's own shared-library auth (cof fetch / run-library) ---
CIRCUITRY_LIBRARY_TOKEN=your-library-auth-token-here

# --- Circuitry settings (optional; override a resolved config value for
#     this shell — see "Where config comes from" in
#     docs/guidebook/04-configuration.md). Commented out: uncomment only
#     the ones you mean to set, each one changes run behaviour.
# CIRCUITRY_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER=ollama
# CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL=http://localhost:11434
# CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL=http://localhost:8188
# CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS=ollama,openai
# CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS=
# CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS=shell,python_eval
# CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT=dev

# --- Persistence and observability runtime plugins (postgres, s3, datadog,
#     sentry, and the rest of docs/runtime-plugins.md) each read their own
#     credential/endpoint env vars (e.g. DATABASE_URL, DD_API_KEY, SENTRY_DSN).
#     There are too many, and the set changes too often, to usefully list
#     here — docs/runtime-plugins.md has one row per plugin naming its env
#     var; `cof doctor` names anything a configured plugin is still missing.
